   "lines": [
    {
     "bbox": [
      310.56,
      62.16,
      335.52,
      70.56
     ],
     "text": "Origin"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      310.8,
      72.24,
      548.16,
      80.64
     ],
     "text": "\u2018Redlands Trailblazer\u2019 arose from a selection and controlled"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      310.08,
      82.08,
      533.52,
      91.2
     ],
     "text": "pollination program between 1978 and 1990. Selection"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      309.84,
      92.4,
      506.88,
      101.28
     ],
     "text": "was primarily for virus resistance and agronomic"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      309.84,
      102.0,
      546.48,
      109.92
     ],
     "text": "characteristics. Resistance was transferred from Cucurbita"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      309.6,
      111.84,
      546.72,
      121.2
     ],
     "text": "ecuadorensis. Following final selection, two generations of"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      309.84,
      121.92,
      545.04,
      129.84
     ],
     "text": "open pollination have established \u2018Redlands Trailblazer\u2019 as"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      309.84,
      131.76,
      345.36,
      139.68
     ],
     "text": "a variety."
    }
   ],
   "page": 1,
   "source": "tesseract-psm3",
   "text": "Origin\n\u2018Redlands Trailblazer\u2019 arose from a selection and controlled\npollination program between 1978 and 1990. Selection\nwas primarily for virus resistance and agronomic\ncharacteristics. Resistance was transferred from Cucurbita\necuadorensis. Following final selection, two generations of\nopen pollination have established \u2018Redlands Trailblazer\u2019 as\na variety.",
   "text_format": "plain",
   "type": "text"
  },
  {
   "bbox": [
    308.88,
    154.32,
    543.6,
    241.92
   ],
   "id": "e10",
   "lines": [
    {
     "bbox": [
      310.08,
      154.32,
      466.56,
      163.2
     ],
     "text": "Morphology \u2014 see comparison tables."
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      309.84,
      164.4,
      520.56,
      173.52
     ],
     "text": "\u2018Redlands Trailblazer\u2019 is an open pollinated vine type"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      309.6,
      174.48,
      530.64,
      183.12
     ],
     "text": "pumpkin. It is resistant to zucchini yellow mosaic virus,"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      309.36,
      184.8,
      538.08,
      193.92
     ],
     "text": "watermelon mosaic virus, and papaya ringspot virus type"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      309.12,
      194.64,
      533.52,
      204.0
     ],
     "text": "W. lt is moderately branched with moderate vigour, and"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      309.36,
      204.96,
      543.6,
      213.84
     ],
     "text": "has medium green, reniform ieaves with no marbling. The"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      309.6,
      214.8,
      522.48,
      222.96
     ],
     "text": "leaves of \u2018Redlands Trailblazer\u2019 are shorter, and have"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      308.88,
      224.64,
      524.64,
      232.8
     ],
     "text": "thinner petioles, than those of \u2018Queensland Blue\u2019 and"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      309.36,
      234.96,
      358.56,
      241.92
     ],
     "text": "\u2018Jarrahdale\u2019."
    }
   ],
   "page": 1,
   "source": "tesseract-psm3",
   "text": "Morphology \u2014 see comparison tables.\n\u2018Redlands Trailblazer\u2019 is an open pollinated vine type\npumpkin. It is resistant to zucchini yellow mosaic virus,\nwatermelon mosaic virus, and papaya ringspot virus type\nW. lt is moderately branched with moderate vigour, and\nhas medium green, reniform ieaves with no marbling. The\nleaves of \u2018Redlands Trailblazer\u2019 are shorter, and have\nthinner petioles, than those of \u2018Queensland Blue\u2019 and\n\u2018Jarrahdale\u2019.",
   "text_format": "plain",
   "type": "text"
  },
  {
   "bbox": [
    308.4,
    259.68,
    532.32,
    296.16
   ],
   "id": "e11",
   "lines": [
    {
     "bbox": [
      309.36,
      259.68,
      528.96,
      267.6
     ],
     "text": "Leaf blades become moderately incised after about the"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      309.12,
      269.52,
      532.32,
      276.72
     ],
     "text": "20th node, but not earlier. \u2018Redtands Trailblazer\u2019 can be"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      308.88,
      279.12,
      528.72,
      287.28
     ],
     "text": "distinguished from \u2018Queensland Blue\u2019 and \u2018Jarrahdale\u2019"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      308.4,
      289.2,
      427.44,
      296.16
     ],
     "text": "which lack this characteristic."
    }
   ],
   "page": 1,
   "source": "tesseract-psm3",
   "text": "Leaf blades become moderately incised after about the\n20th node, but not earlier. \u2018Redtands Trailblazer\u2019 can be\ndistinguished from \u2018Queensland Blue\u2019 and \u2018Jarrahdale\u2019\nwhich lack this characteristic.",
   "text_format": "plain",
   "type": "text"
  },
